### 4. SOVEREIGN IDENTITY PROVISION
This software implements cryptographic identity systems (NFA_V6 addresses,
sovereign keyrings, zero-knowledge proofs). These identity systems are
designed to be:
- Self-custodial (user holds their own keys)
- Hardware-bound (DNA binding to physical device)
- Burn-on-consume (keys self-destruct after single use)
- Anonymous by default (no central authority can deanonymize users)

Users of this software are sovereign individuals. This software makes no
assertions about the legal status of any cryptographic identity, and
users are solely responsible for compliance with local laws.

### 5. OPEN SOURCE COMMITMENT
All source code, cryptographic primitives, and mathematical specifications
in this repository are released under the terms of this license. There
are no backdoors, no hidden master keys, and no remote kill switches.
The protocol is fully auditable and reproducible.

